  "content": "• Similarity: similar figures and their properties\n• Linear scale factor of similar figures\n• Area scale factor of similar figures\n• Volume scale factor of similar solids\n• Enlargement: centre of enlargement and scale factor\n• Constructing images under enlargement (positive, negative and fractional scale factors)\n• Finding the centre and scale factor of an enlargement from an object and its image\n• Application of similarity and enlargement in real life (scale drawings, maps, photographs, models)",
  "learningOutcomes": "By the end of the sub-strand, the learner should be able to:\na) identify similar figures in the environment,\nb) state the properties of similar figures,\nc) determine the linear scale factor of similar figures,\nd) determine the area scale factor of similar figures,\ne) determine the volume scale factor of similar solids,\nf) construct the image of an object under enlargement given the centre and the scale factor,\ng) determine the centre and the scale factor of an enlargement,\nh) apply similarity and enlargement in real-life situations,\ni) appreciate the use of similarity and enlargement in day-to-day activities.",
  "coreCompetencies": "• Communication and Collaboration: learners discuss with peers to identify similar figures, justify scale factors and share enlargement constructions in groups.\n• Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: learners reason about why a photo resizes without distortion, and use scale factors to solve length, area and volume problems.\n• Creativity and Imagination: learners design scale drawings and enlarged or reduced images of familiar objects, such as school logos and passport photos.\n• Digital Literacy: learners use digital devices or geometry software to enlarge and reduce images and to check scale factors where available.",
