        "teacherMoves": "Hold up the three cut-outs and say: 'Wanjiru's face is the same in all three. Mr Otieno at Lakeview Photo Studio needs one number to tell his printer how much to shrink or stretch. What number would you give him?' Give WAIT TIME of 10-15 seconds of silent thinking before anyone writes. Then ask partners to share for 1 minute. Cold-call 4 learners with different predictions and record all of them on the board without judging. Ask: 'Who has a different number? What did you compare to get it?' Note any learners who compare only the width, or who subtract (14 − 3.5) instead of dividing.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Prediction with Think-Pair-Share: committing to a prediction first creates a need to know and surfaces the common subtraction misconception ('10.5 cm smaller') so that later evidence can be compared with learners' own ideas. Learners see that they need a way to compare sizes as a multiplier rather than a difference.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Listen for learners who use multiplication or division ('about 4 times smaller') rather than subtraction. Check that at least 3 of the 4 cold-called learners can say which print they compared from and which to. Tally on the board how many predicted 4, 5, or 'don't know'. Look for who expects the same factor for the distorted print."
