    "overview": "Mrs Achieng opens by returning to Wanjiru Atieno's photographs from Lakeview Photo Studio in Kisumu. Learners first predict individually how they would convince Mr Otieno, the photographer, why the 3.5 × 4.5 cm passport photo is faithful but the 4.5 × 4.5 cm print is not. In the Observe phase, groups re-examine the four prints (14 × 18, 3.5 × 4.5, 70 × 90, 4.5 × 4.5 cm) and complete a one-page evidence table of width : height ratios, scale factors, chin angles and area factors using their own earlier measurements. In the Explain phase, groups write a claim-evidence-reasoning Final Explanation and test it against a new challenge. Then the class resolves the Driving Question Board, and finally learners revise their cumulative model and compare it with their Lesson 1 model, noting what changed in their thinking. The lesson ends by connecting the idea to the two KICD Key Inquiry Questions.",
