        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'A good explanation has a claim, evidence and reasoning. Your reasoning must explain WHY, using the words corresponding sides, corresponding angles and scale factor k.' Provide a sentence frame: 'The passport photo is similar to the original because ___; the distorted print is not similar because ___.' Give WAIT TIME of 10-15 seconds, then circulate asking: 'You say the shape is kept. What exactly is kept?' and 'If I only changed the width, which number in your evidence changes?' Pose the Transfer Challenge and give 4 minutes. Select 3 groups to present (cold-call: 'Group 2, please read your reasoning'). After each, ask a different group: 'Do you agree? Which piece of evidence convinces you?' Allow challenge from the class. Then synthesise on the board: 'What stays the same: ratios of corresponding sides, corresponding angles. What changes: lengths (by k), area (by k²), volume (by k³).' Briefly link Lesson 5 (shadow triangles: Wanjiru 1.5 m, shadow 2 m; tree, shadow 12 m, height 9 m) as another place where equal angles give proportional sides, without re-teaching.",
