        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Mrs Achieng's board has been waiting since Lesson 1. Let us see which questions we can now answer with evidence.' Hand each group 2 or 3 cards. Give WAIT TIME of 10-15 seconds when a group reads a question aloud before they respond. Ask: 'Which lesson gave you the evidence?' and 'Can you answer using k, ratios or angles?' Cold-call 4 groups to read and defend one answer each. For the KICD Key Inquiry Questions, pose them directly: 'Why do we need to enlarge or reduce objects?' (passport photos, posters, maps like Kisumu to Nairobi, sign painting) and 'How do we use similarity and enlargement in day-to-day activities?' (shadows to find the height of a tree: 9 m; scale drawings; costing a sign: area factor 9 gives KES 2268). Mark any questions not yet answered as 'to be explored in 2.2 Reflection and Congruence' (note that k = 1 gives an identical size, which is studied later).",
