        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Take out your Lesson 1 model. Now complete your final model so that it explains what Mr Otieno did right and what went wrong with the 4.5 by 4.5 print.' Insist that every arrow has a scale factor and the units are cm. Give WAIT TIME of 10-15 seconds after the prompt 'What is the biggest change between your two models?' before taking answers. Cold-call 3 learners to read their 'In Lesson 1 I thought... Now I know...' sentences. Use probing questions: 'Where does your model show why the chin angle changed?' and 'Where does your model show area changing by k²?' Conclude with a 2-minute exit slip: 'In one sentence, what must stay the same and what is allowed to change when a photo is resized?' Expected: the ratios of corresponding sides and the angles must stay the same (one scale factor for all lengths); size, lengths and area may change.",
